  "description": "EVO PDF Merge Library for .NET (Classic) can be used in .NET Framework, .NET Core and .NET Standard applications on Windows to merge multiple PDF documents into a single PDF document.\n\nFor Windows, Linux and macOS, the Core PDF API of EvoPdf Next creates, edits, merges and secures PDF documents. It comes in the multi-platform package EvoPdf.Next.Core and the platform packages EvoPdf.Next.Core.Windows (x64 and ARM64), EvoPdf.Next.Core.Linux (x64 and ARM64) and EvoPdf.Next.Core.MacOS (ARM64).\n\nThe full EvoPdf Next library, which also converts HTML, Word, Excel, RTF and Markdown to PDF, comes in the EvoPdf.Next, EvoPdf.Next.Windows, EvoPdf.Next.Windows.Arm64, EvoPdf.Next.Linux, EvoPdf.Next.Linux.Arm64 and EvoPdf.Next.MacOS packages.\n\nCompatibility:\n\n* .NET Framework 4.0 and above\n* .NET 10, 9, 8, 7, 6 and .NET Standard 2.0\n* Windows platforms\n* Azure App Service\n* Azure Cloud Services and Azure Virtual Machines\n* Web, Console and Desktop applications\n\nMain Features:\n\n* Merge PDF documents from files and streams\n* Specify the range of PDF pages to be merged from each PDF document\n* Save the merged document in memory or to a file\n* Merge PDF bookmarks\n* Set the compression level of the resulting PDF document\n* Set merged document information (title, author, creation date)\n* Password-protect the merged document\n* Set merged document rights for printing, copying and assembling",
